-- pause.flang — what the pause menu's buttons do.
--
-- On the screen rather than on each button, for the reason menu.flang gives:
-- a click bubbles from the widget to its screen when the widget has no script
-- of its own, so one handler serves all of them and `src.id` tells them apart.
--
-- Resume is spelled out here even though Escape already does it. Escape is the
-- stack's own doing — it closes the topmost modal screen (Stack.Cancel) — and a
-- menu that can only be dismissed by a key is not one a pointer can leave.

def on_click(:click:, src ref) when src.id == "resume" -> null
    hide_screen("pause")

on_click(:click:, src ref) when src.id == "to_menu"
    -- Back to the main menu, which is modal and pausing in its own right, so
    -- the level stays frozen behind it. Deliberately NOT a reload: the player
    -- is put back where they stood when Play is pressed again. Restarting the
    -- level would mean load_level, and a load resets the screen stack — the
    -- menu would be swept off it before the new level was up.
    hide_screen("pause")
    show_screen("menu")

on_click(:click:, src ref) when src.id == "quit"
    quit_game()

on_click(:click:, src ref)
    -- Any other widget on this screen, including one added later. Doing
    -- nothing is the right answer; taking the menu down would not be.
    return
end
